  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0026_257e6d249b93.jpg\" /><br /><br />In the case of equilibrium, net force on the piston becomes zero. So,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PA</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Kx</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Kx</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>Kx</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>"
